Issue 3: Inconsistent Text Cleaning

You have scattered .replace() calls. Create a single sanitization function.

Fix - Add this function at the top of your script (around line 1200, after other utility functions):

```javascript
// Single source of truth for text sanitization
function sanitizeText(text) {
    if (!text || typeof text !== 'string') return '';
    // Remove control characters and normalize spaces
    return text
        .replace(/[^\x20-\x7E\u00A0-\u00FF]/g, '')  // Keep printable chars only
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')                        // Normalize whitespace
        .trim();
}
```

Then, inside exportToPDF, replace the addWrappedText function's cleaning with a call to this function:

```javascript
function addWrappedText(doc, text, x, y, maxWidth, lineHeight, fontStyle = 'normal') {
    if (!text || text === 'undefined') return y;
    
    let cleanedContent = sanitizeText(text);  // <-- USE THE SINGLE FUNCTION
    
    if (cleanedContent.length === 0) return y;
    
    doc.setFont(undefined, fontStyle);
    const lines = doc.splitTextToSize(cleanedContent, maxWidth);
    doc.text(lines, x, y);
    return y + (lines.length * lineHeight);
}
```

